WEBVTT

00:02:28.538 --> 00:02:30.788
infant development.

00:02:31.038 --> 00:02:33.663
So, understanding the way
infants develop into children,

00:02:33.704 --> 00:02:36.246
develop to adults,
and how they learn and interact

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.788
is actually important for robotics.

00:02:38.996 --> 00:02:41.413
I didn't understand
that I'd actually have to watch

00:02:41.454 --> 00:02:43.996
tapes of monkeys
interacting and communicating,

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:46.371
because they have
a whole social kind of mechanism

00:02:46.413 --> 00:02:48.788
where they learn from each other,

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:51.163
and so that's really good
to make robots smarter.

00:02:51.288 --> 00:02:54.413
And, of course, neuroscience,
I’ve always been fascinated with it,

00:02:54.454 --> 00:02:56.663
but I never understood
that I had to figure out

00:02:56.704 --> 00:02:57.996
why do the neurons fire,

00:02:58.038 --> 00:03:01.204
what about the environment
helps us to learn,